# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the Duet3 6HC (SAME70Q20B) over its REAL
# USB-CDC host link, in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. This is the USB-CDC
# sibling of duet3_6hc.test: same duet3-6hc pin map, same four TMC5160s on
# the shared usart1 SPI daisy-chain (chain_length 6, renode_hooks TMC SPI
# chain responder), same adc_scaled vref/vssa-compensated AFEC thermistors,
# same interactive gcode - but klippy connects over the synthetic USBHS
# BULK_IN/BULK_OUT pipe (CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware, same70q20b-usb.dict)
# instead of the serial-mode UART2 substitute.
#
# The real Duet3 6HC is USB+CAN only, so this exercises the host link the
# board actually ships with. duet3_6hc.test had to fall back to the
# serial-mode build because the SAME70 USB tick byte-shuttle was unusable
# during identify: the renode pty advanced a full QMAX (100 ms) of
# simulated time per host<->mcu round trip, so the identify dictionary scan
# plus the SPI-chain / AFEC config phase took far too long in simulated
# time and the link drifted. klippy/serialhdl.py now registers the
# serialqueue_need_prompt predicate for every tick MCU (not just the simavr
# AF_UNIX socket), so identify / clock-sync / config round trips advance at
# the small QWAIT (8 ms) quantum and complete promptly over USB-CDC, while
# streaming still coalesces at QMAX. Motion-free, as with the other
# per-printer tests.
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG duet3_6hc.cfg
EMULATOR duet3_6hc_usb.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped both ends of the chain (pos 1 / pos 4); IOIN
# version=0x30 proves the SPI chain read path round-tripped over USB-CDC.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x30"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ZeroDivisionError"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
